# Development standards

This repository is primarily documentation and agent-kit Markdown. When editing here or related Nortiqa code elsewhere, apply:

## Clarity

- Prefer readable, explicit structure over cleverness.
- Use clear names for files, roles (`NL-*`), and sections.
- Keep functions/sections small and single-purpose when writing scripts or code.
- Comments only when they add non-obvious context (why, not what).

## Architecture fit

- Inspect before modifying. Prefer compatibility with the existing kit (`agents/`, handoffs, autonomy zones).
- Do not invent parallel canons, second memory roots, or duplicate role systems.
- Map external labels (e.g. NQ-DEV-IMPLEMENTER) onto existing `NL-*` roles instead of renaming the kit.
- Prefer dependencies and patterns already used in the target repo; do not add new stacks to this org-profile repo without Gio/audit intent.

## Quality bar

- Primero funcional. Después excelente.
- Small, reversible, verifiable diffs.
- Explicit error handling in any scripts; fail loudly with actionable messages.
- Minimize duplication: link to `AGENTS.md`, `SHARED_RULES.md`, `AUTONOMY.md` rather than copying long policy blocks.
- Typing: when working in typed languages in other Nortiqa repos, follow that repo’s existing type/lint config (not invented here).

## Anti-patterns

- Designing “humo” without verifiable utility
- Overwriting existing configs without analysis
- Broad refactors during configuration or unrelated tasks
- Mixing entity branding, domains, or credentials
